marta-docs: Heads up — external SOC2 auditor asked for a minimal reproducible 'audit log export' example that shows redaction semantics and retention metadata. They want both a curl JSONL export and a streaming Node example. Can we add both to docs/security/audit-exports.md?

lena-legal: @marta-docs can you paste the exact wording they requested? we should avoid implying we store PII longer than policy allows. :eyes:

marta-docs: here's the ask from auditor (pasted): "Provide a sample export showing (1) event-level timestamps, (2) pseudonymized user ids, (3) a field-level redaction marker (e.g. \"redacted:true\"), and (4) retention_ttl metadata in seconds." They also asked for example language for customers: what 'export scope' covers.

raj-eng: ok. for the curl example i can do a tiny JSONL output with redaction marker. thinking of adding a note about streaming vs paged exports. sample snippet: ```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY" -H "Accept: application/x-ndjson" https://api.redwood.ai/v1/audit/export?start=2025-11-01T00:00:00Z
```
And then show sample lines like: ```jsonl
{"ts":"2025-11-01T12:00:00Z","event":"login","user_id":"pseud-123","redacted":false,"retention_ttl_seconds":7776000}
{"ts":"2025-11-01T12:05:00Z","event":"request","user_id":"pseud-999","redacted":true,"redaction_reason":"PII","retention_ttl_seconds":7776000}
```

oliver-sdk: I can add a Node streaming example that pipes to a file and handles incremental flush/redaction markers. something like: ```js
const https = require('https');
const fs = require('fs');
const out = fs.createWriteStream('audit-export.ndjson');
const req = https.request({
  hostname: 'api.redwood.ai',
  path: '/v1/audit/export?start=2025-11-01T00:00:00Z',
  headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_KEY}` , 'Accept': 'application/x-ndjson' }
}, res => {
  res.pipe(out);
});
req.end();
```
I'll keep it minimal and call out that the SDK wrappers exist but this is raw HTTP for auditors.

lena-legal: wording suggestion for customer-facing docs: "Export scope: includes tenant-level audit events generated by the Redwood inference control plane (authentication, model deployment, access to audit endpoints). It excludes application-layer logs and request bodies unless explicitly enabled by the customer. Exports include per-event retention metadata and a redaction flag where sensitive fields have been pseudonymized or removed." Don't promise more than we deliver.

marta-docs: Nice. Can you also add a short paragraph about how retention_ttl_seconds relates to our retention policy (e.g., "values shown are illustrative; actual retention depends on plan and legal holds")?

lena-legal: yes add: "Retention TTL in examples is illustrative. Actual retention is governed by customer contract and applicable legal obligations; legal holds can override TTLs."

raj-eng: QA question: should the example show both pseudonymization and full redaction? i.e., user_id pseud-### vs user_email redacted? auditor asked for field-level marker — i think showing both is helpful.

marta-docs: agreed. i'll include one line with pseudonymized id and one with redacted email + redaction_reason. also add a tiny table describing fields and sensitivity level (public, internal, sensitive).

ci-bot: New PR opened by marta-docs: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4123 — includes curl + node examples, field table, and legal phrasing. Assigns reviewers: @lena-legal, @oliver-sdk.

lena-legal: reviewing now. quick flag: replace "redaction_reason" value "PII" with enumerated reasons we use ("PII","LEGAL_HOLD","CUSTOMER_REQUEST"). will post exact enum in review comments.

oliver-sdk: looks good to me. small nit: in Node example, swap to streaming with backpressure handling snippet? but keep main example simple. happy to add an appendix for robust consumers.

marta-docs: thanks all. i'll patch PR per comments and add a short note linking to the audit schema doc and to the retention policy. target merge by EOD tomorrow. :+1:

raj-eng: if you want i can add a small test vector to the repo that asserts exported NDJSON has required fields.

marta-docs: yes please do that as a follow-up PR. tagging this thread for visibility.

oliver-sdk: :+1:

lena-legal: approved pending enum tweak.

marta-docs: will update now and request final review. thanks everyone!
